<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1">
  <DUT Name="ST_DeviceStateTable" Id="{03fca704-e94f-069c-15d5-ec1df795b0de}">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[(*
ST_DeviceStateTable - one state row of a device state table.

Purpose:
    Describes the setpoint a single device state commands: which device the row
    belongs to (iDeviceID) and which state it is (iStateID), the target position
    with the tolerance band around it, and the beam parameters that state
    requires (transmission, beam class, pulse rate, per-pulse energy and photon
    energy range). The row is the shared contract between the configuration
    source of the state table and the device logic that consumes it.

Usage:
    Fill one instance per device state and hand it to the device state logic that
    commands the hardware. Every engineering value states its unit in the comment
    next to it: a setpoint written in different units is applied silently and
    mis-commands the device, so convert before writing the row.

History:
    2020-06-25 A. Wallace - initial declaration
    2026-11-27            - header comment added, member meanings and units documented
*)
TYPE ST_DeviceStateTable :
STRUCT
    iDeviceID : DINT; // Device this state row belongs to (device table key)
    iStateID : DINT; // State key within that device's state table
    rTargetPosition : REAL; // Commanded position of the device axis, in mm
    rTolerance : REAL; // Allowed +/- band around rTargetPosition, in mm
    rTransmission : REAL; // Required beam transmission fraction, 0.0 (blocked) .. 1.0 (full)
    iBeamClass : DINT; // Required beam class code, see E_MPSBeamClasses (0 = beam off)
    iPulseRate : DINT; // Required beam pulse repetition rate, in Hz (0 = no beam)
    rPerPulseEnergy : REAL; // Required beam energy per pulse, in mJ
    rUpper_eV : REAL; // Upper bound of the required photon energy range, in eV
    rLower_eV : REAL; // Lower bound of the required photon energy range, in eV
    rPhotonEnergy : REAL; // Required photon energy, in eV
END_STRUCT
END_TYPE
]]></Declaration>
  </DUT>
</TcPlcObject>